# Credentials — NEVER commit. Copy .env.example to .env and fill in.
.env
*.pem

# Customer evidence (filenames contain customer names) and browser profiles
# (contain logged-in sessions/cookies).
ScreenShot*/
screen_shot/
sites_scan_google/
user_data/
assets/

# Virtualenv.
#
# On Windows the venv lives in the pipeline root itself, and the filesystem is
# case-insensitive — so `Lib\` (venv) and `lib\` (our 8 custom modules) are the
# SAME directory. That is why only `site-packages` is excluded here and never
# `lib/` or `Lib/` wholesale: ignoring the directory would drop
# broker_helpers.py, automation_delay.py, captcha.py, common.py,
# email_sender.py, email_verification.py, proxies.py and safe_browser.py from
# the repo, and manage.py will not start without them.
Lib/site-packages/
lib/site-packages/
Include/
Scripts/
pyvenv.cfg

# Belt and braces: the custom modules are tracked no matter what.
!lib/*.py
!Lib/*.py

# Runtime state and junk
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
*.bak.*
*.bak-*
dump.rdb
*.rdb
ccpa_email_counter.json
captcha.png
__downloaded.mp3
info.jpeg
extension.zip
pkgs.txt
